WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.600
Here's how to connect your own LiveKit to Jobak, so you can practise interviews out loud. Start by opening your project in LiveKit Cloud.

2
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.250
Open Settings, then General.

3
00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:17.417
Under Options, find Development token server. It starts switched off.

4
00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:26.423
Turn it on, then copy the Token server ID that appears. Keep it private: anyone who has it can start calls on your account.

5
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:34.383
Next, create the interviewer. In Agents, choose Create agent, then Create in browser using Agent Builder.

6
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:38.290
Pick the one-to-one training template, and press Create.

7
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:55.330
On the Conversation tab, replace the instructions and the welcome message with ours. Jobak has a copy button for each. A red warning about unrecognized variables is expected: it goes away once you add the variables on the Advanced tab.

8
00:00:55.883 --> 00:01:06.283
Then, on the Actions tab, add a client tool named submit evaluation, and paste our description. This is how the interviewer sends you feedback at the end.

9
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:17.390
Add the four parameters with Jobak's copy buttons: score as an integer, and summary, strengths and mistakes as strings. Turn Silent on, and press Add tool.

10
00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:29.910
On the Advanced tab, give the agent a name, like jobak interviewer. Then, under Custom metadata, add four text variables: role, company, job description, and candidate name.

11
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:36.460
On Models and Voice, you can keep the default realtime model, or choose a different voice.

12
00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:41.327
Press Deploy agent, and wait until the deployment has completed.

13
00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:59.133
Back in Jobak, paste the token server ID and the agent name, and press Connect. Then start your practice interview. When you're done, press Finish and get feedback, to see your score and every mistake, with a better answer for each, and a PDF to download. Good luck!

